+# Google Play release guide
+
+## Build the bundle
+```bash
+flutter pub get
+dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
+flutter analyze && flutter test
+flutter build appbundle --release --flavor play --dart-define=PLAY_BUILD=true
+# -> build/app/outputs/bundle/playRelease/app-play-release.aab
+```
+Bump `version:` in `pubspec.yaml` first; `+N` is the Play versionCode and must increase on every upload.
+
+## Signing
+Use Play App Signing (default). Sign the AAB with your existing upload key (`android/key.properties`, `~/.android/pagemark-release.jks`) or generate a new upload key. Back the keystore up. **The sideload APK and the Play build will be signed by different keys**, so existing GitHub-APK users cannot update in place to the Play version (uninstall/restore from backup).
+
+## Drive backup on Play builds
+Google sign-in needs an Android OAuth client using the **Play App Signing SHA-1** (Play Console -> Test and release -> App signing) in addition to your upload-key SHA-1. Update `docs/DRIVE_SETUP.md` steps accordingly. Test backup from a Play internal-testing install.
+
+## Developer account
+One-time $25. New personal accounts must run a **closed test with 12+ testers for 14 consecutive days** before applying for production. Start this early.
+
+## Store listing
+- **App name:** Pagemark
+- **Short description (80):** Private, offline book tracker. Log reads, rate, and keep your thoughts.
+- **Full description:** Pagemark is a private, fully local book tracker. Log what you read or listen to (print, e-book, audiobook), rate it, track progress and goals, and keep private thoughts. Search Open Library, scan an ISBN barcode, or add by hand. Organise with shelves, series and tags. Lock a private library behind a PIN or fingerprint. Export CSV/JSON, back up to your own Google Drive, restore safely. No accounts, no ads, no analytics.
+- **Category:** Books & Reference. **Contact email + privacy policy URL:** https://github.com/AxialForge/Pagemark/blob/main/docs/PRIVACY.md
+- **Graphics needed:** icon 512x512 PNG, feature graphic 1024x500, 2-8 phone screenshots (use the light-theme ones in `docs/screenshots/`).
+
+## Data safety form (verify each answer in Console)
+- Data collected by the developer: **None.**
+- Data shared: ISBN/title search text goes to Open Library (third-party service, no identifiers). Declare per current Play guidance for user-initiated lookups.
+- Drive backup: user-initiated transfer to the user's own Google account.
+- Security: data encrypted in transit (HTTPS); users can request deletion (uninstall / Drive settings).
+- No ads. Content rating questionnaire: no violence/sexual content/etc. -> expect Everyone. Target audience: 13+ or 18+ (not children).
+
+## Permissions
+INTERNET, CAMERA (barcode scan), USE_BIOMETRIC (vault). `REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES` is stripped in the play flavor.
+
+## Pre-submit checks
+- [ ] `flutter build appbundle --flavor play` succeeds; merged manifest has no REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES (`bundletool` or Android Studio manifest viewer)
+- [ ] Settings shows "Version history", no Updates tile
+- [ ] Release install on a real phone: scan, biometrics, Drive backup/restore, export
+- [ ] Verify targetSdk meets Play's current requirement (Flutter's default tracks it)
